      "finding": "--ipc=host",
      "explanation": "Potential security issue detected. Manual review is recommended.",
      "remediation": "Review the flagged content for security risks. Ensure no credentials, secrets, or sensitive data are exposed.",
      "code_snippet": "`2.9.0a0+50eac811a6.nv25.09`, CUDA 13.0 baked in, matches the ABI Rule's expectations — no functional delta observed for the packages exercised in fine-tuning workflows). Treat `SKILL.md`'s mention of a newer blessed tag as guidance to pull when locally available, not a hard requirement — if the cited newer tag isn't locally cached and pulling isn't practical, fall back to the newest available `25.x` tag and record the gap in the run's notes rather than blocking on it.\n\n- `--runtime=nvidia --gpus all` gives the container access to the GB10 GPU; without it, PyTorch inside the container will report no CUDA device even though the host sees one fine.\n- `--ipc=host` and the `ulimit` flags avoid shared-memory starvation for PyTorch's DataLoader workers.\n- Mount the repo's `finetuning/` run directory so checkpoints and logs land on the host filesystem, not inside the ephemeral container layer — the `--rm` flag deletes the container (and anything not mounted out) on exit.\n\n## Unsloth container",
      "intent": null,
      "tags": [
        "Privilege Escalation"
      ],
